/-- Sigma-algebra generated by a finite block of sample coordinates.

For an abstract sample family indexed by `I`, this is the measurable space on
the base probability space generated by the finitely many coordinates listed in
`block`.

Layer: Model | Concept: Filtration
Proof: (definitional construction; finite indexed supremum of coordinate
  comap sigma-algebras)
Source: Mathlib measure-theory measurable-space comap and complete-lattice APIs
Used in: nonconvex stochastic mirror descent randomized-output validation
  freshness through its finite optimization sample footprint
Book citation: book/FOML/NonconvexStochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec
Origin algorithm: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for
  Machine Learning, nonconvex stochastic mirror descent -/
@[reducible]
noncomputable def sampleBlockMeasurableSpace
    {Ω S I : Type*} [MeasurableSpace S]
    (ξ : I → Ω → S) (block : Finset I) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ q : {q // q ∈ block},
    MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => ξ q.1 ω)
      (by infer_instance : MeasurableSpace S)

