@[reducible]
noncomputable def strictPastSampleBlockMeasurableSpace
    {Ω Ξ : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ξ]
    (ξ : ℕ → Ω → Ξ) (idx : ℕ × ℕ × ℕ → ℕ)
    (block : Finset (ℕ × ℕ × ℕ)) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ q : {q // q ∈ block},
    MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => ξ (idx q.1) ω)
      (by infer_instance : MeasurableSpace Ξ)

/-- A coordinate in a finite sample block is measurable for the sigma-algebra
generated by that block.

For a sample stream `ξ`, an abstract coordinate indexer `idx`, and a finite
block of coordinates, the selected coordinate is one of the generators in the
finite-block supremum.

Layer: Model | Gap: Level 0 (sample-coordinate measurability in generated finite block filtration)
Proof: rewrite measurability as a `comap`-subspace inequality and include the
  selected coordinate generator into the indexed supremum with `le_iSup`.
Source: Mathlib measure-theory measurable-space comap and complete-lattice APIs
Used in: nonconvex stochastic mirror descent strict-past mini-batch sample
  filtration for iterate measurability
Book citation: book/FOML/NonconvexStochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec
Origin algorithm: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for
  Machine Learning, nonconvex stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem sampleBlock_coordinate_measurable
    {Ω Ξ β : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ξ]
    (ξ : ℕ → Ω → Ξ) (idx : β → ℕ) (block : Finset β)
    {q : β} (hq : q ∈ block) :
    Measurable[
      ⨆ q' : {q // q ∈ block},
        MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => ξ (idx q'.1) ω)
          (by infer_instance : MeasurableSpace Ξ)]
      (fun ω => ξ (idx q) ω) := by
  exact measurable_iff_comap_le.mpr (by
    simpa using
      le_iSup
        (fun q' : {q // q ∈ block} =>
          MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => ξ (idx q'.1) ω)
            (by infer_instance : MeasurableSpace Ξ))
        ⟨q, hq⟩)

/-- Every coordinate in a finite sample block is measurable for the sigma-algebra generated by that block.

The coordinate subspace appears as one generator in the finite-block supremum,
so measurability follows by the universal order characterization of `comap`.

Layer: Model | Gap: Level 0 (sample-coordinate measurability in generated block filtration)
Proof: rewrite measurability as a `comap`-subspace inequality and include the
  selected coordinate generator into the indexed supremum with `le_iSup`.
Source: Mathlib measure-theory measurable-space comap and complete-lattice APIs
Used in: nonconvex stochastic mirror descent strict-past mini-batch sample
  filtration for iterate measurability
Book citation: book/FOML/NonconvexStochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec
Origin algorithm: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for
  Machine Learning, nonconvex stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem strictPastSampleBlockMeasurableSpace_coordinate_measurable
    {Ω Ξ : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ξ]
    (ξ : ℕ → Ω → Ξ) (idx : ℕ × ℕ × ℕ → ℕ)
    (block : Finset (ℕ × ℕ × ℕ)) {q : ℕ × ℕ × ℕ}
    (hq : q ∈ block) :
    Measurable[strictPastSampleBlockMeasurableSpace ξ idx block]
      (fun ω => ξ (idx q) ω) := by
  unfold strictPastSampleBlockMeasurableSpace
  exact sampleBlock_coordinate_measurable ξ idx block hq

